From 77365ec843d6ebd988eee2a8e69588a0d0a2c578 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kumar Ankit <186563577+krank-09@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:37:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] feat: show the audit record's data visually instead of a
 network diagram

Drops the sender/receiver diagram (the same in nearly every record) for pictures of the record's own JSON: summary tiles, evidence meter, token delivery, test-token bars per route, error rate with its interval against the honest and eavesdropper levels, each verifier's contradictions plus a checklist of its checks, the circuit-breaker change (before -> after), a timeline, and record integrity with the rules used and the fidelity estimate. Facts gain the matching fields. An acceptance above the first-stage limit is labelled as passing the reserve stage. Without facts (e.g. an old server) the visuals are omitted rather than drawn with placeholders.
---
